2461	/// Render one `Setup:` policy cell: the token, marked when CPUs disagree, or why it is absent.
2462	///
2463	/// - `None` prints `not exposed` and never a default. A box without the file has no such
2464	///   policy, and inventing one is exactly what makes an archived number ambiguous.
2465	/// - A non-uniform field carries `(mixed across CPUs)`: one CPU's token is not the box's policy
2466	///   when the policy groups were set separately.
2467	fn policy_cell(field: Option<&freq::PolicyField>) -> String {
2468	    match field {
2469	        None => "not exposed".to_string(),
2470	        Some(f) if f.uniform => f.value.clone(),
2471	        Some(f) => format!("{} (mixed across CPUs)", f.value),
2472	    }
2473	}
